{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "FP605 industrial fan and pump drive (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "fp605",
  "short_model": "FP605",
  "aliases": [
    "CIPR-FP6",
    "FP605 drive",
    "FP605 AC Drive for Industrial Fan and Pump Applications"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa FP605 drives using the built-in RS-485 port (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU), per technical reference SIEPC7106171F.",
  "summary": "Yaskawa's drive for industrial fans and pumps, with a built-in RS-485 port running MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU. Command registers (run bits, frequency reference, PID setpoints, digital outputs) start at 0001H, status and monitor registers at 0020H, and every parameter is reachable at the hex number printed under it. This map covers the command and status words, the key monitors, fault bits and the b1/H5 setup parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 31,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are hex and are sent unchanged: the manual's read example (Table 6.7) asks slave 2 for starting register 0020H as bytes 00 20. Parameters use the hex number printed under each parameter (H5-01 = 0425H)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "FP605 Drive AC Drive for Industrial Fan and Pump Applications Technical Reference",
    "doc_number": "SIEPC7106171FE",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPC7106171F&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPC7106171F.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 6.3 MEMOBUS/Modbus Communications pp. 277-300: Table 6.2 specs, Table 6.3 b1 settings, Table 6.5 function codes, Table 6.7 read example, Table 6.13 Enter commands, Table 6.15 command data pp. 288-293, Table 6.16 monitor data pp. 294-300; b1 parameters p. 515; H5 parameters pp. 871-875."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Frequency registers 0002H, 0023H and 0024H use the units chosen in o1-03, so they are left unscaled.",
    "Left out: 0025H output voltage (unit switched by H5-10), 0026H output current and 00ABH rated current (the manual says the rated-current unit differs by model), 0027H output power and 0028H/0032H torque reference (unit/sign not fixed in the table), 003EH/003FH and 00B5H-00B8H speed/frequency monitors in r/min or 0.01 % (sign not stated), the U-monitor, fault-trace and fault-history blocks from 0040H, the FP605 smart-network block 1A7FH-1AA0H, the real-time-clock registers 3004H-3030H and the emergency-override registers 3A93H-3A96H.",
    "Supported function codes are 03H, 08H, 10H, 5AH and 67H (non-consecutive read/write); there is no 06H, so use 10H even for a single register.",
    "U4-01 cumulative operation time is split over two 16-bit registers (0098H = value / 10, 0099H = last digit), not a 32-bit value.",
    "With H5-11 = 0, parameters written over Modbus take effect only after the Enter command (0900H or 0910H). Command registers 0001H-001FH do not need Enter."
  ],
